SiliconWin: hvf: skip memory sections that are not page aligned

Attaching a TPM (tpm-tis-device) under HVF crashes QEMU with HV_BAD_ARGUMENT
on Apple silicon: the TPM's 1 KiB PPI buffer is not aligned to the host's
16 KiB pages, so it was never mapped, yet QEMU still tried to unmap it. Leave
such sections alone; they are handled as MMIO.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later, like the file it modifies (accel/hvf/hvf-all.c).

--- a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c	2026-10-03 05:28:07
+++ b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c	2026-10-03 05:28:07
@@ -113,8 +113,14 @@
 
     if (!QEMU_IS_ALIGNED(size, page_size) ||
         !QEMU_IS_ALIGNED(gpa, page_size)) {
-        /* Not page aligned, so we can not map as RAM */
-        add = false;
+        /*
+         * Not page aligned, so we can not map as RAM. Such a section was never
+         * mapped either (e.g. the 1 KiB TPM PPI buffer on 16 KiB-page Apple
+         * silicon), so there is nothing to unmap: calling hv_vm_unmap() with
+         * unaligned arguments fails with HV_BAD_ARGUMENT and aborts QEMU.
+         * Guest accesses simply trap to QEMU instead. (SiliconWin patch)
+         */
+        return;
     }
 
     if (!add) {
